  - Second command-line parameter is the playing-field side length; it must be at least 5 and odd.
  - A die roll must always be computed as random.nextInt(6) + 1.
  - nextInt should only be called when a die roll is actually required, to preserve the
  deterministic sequence.
  - Interactive program outputs must match the specification exactly, including case, spaces and
  newlines, and no extra information may be printed.
  - The user interface must be case-insensitive (input case is ignored).
  - Die Aktion propel ist nur verfügbar, wenn das Raumschiff ein Propulsion-Modul besitzt.
  - Ramm darf nur eingesetzt werden, wenn das angreifende Raumschiff keine Waffen-Module mehr hat.
  - A Collector always has exactly one Engine module and otherwise only the special Container
  module.
  - Other ships always have an Engine as their first module.
  - Per ship, the number of Weapon modules must be at most 2.
  - Program code must be written in English.
  - Submitted program code must compile without errors.
  - After printing an error message the program should continue and wait for the next input.
  - Every error message must begin with 'Error,' and must not contain special characters such as
  newlines or umlauts.
  - You may choose English text freely for error messages, but they should be meaningful.
  </adaptive_rules>

