  - The implementation must use exactly one fixed instance of the Random generator to ensure a
  deterministic sequence.
  - Interactive program outputs must match the specification exactly, including case, spaces and
  newlines, and no extra information may be printed.
  - The user interface must be case-insensitive (input case is ignored).
  - Adhere to the JavaDoc documentation rules.
  - All whitespace rules must be followed.
  - Calls to System.exit(), Runtime.exit() or similar must not be used.
  - Choose appropriate visibilities for classes, methods, and attributes.
  - Do not use the default package.
