  - Submitted program code must compile without errors.
  - The online submission requires individual submission of *.java files with the correct folder
  structure.
  - Use System.in for input and System.out for output unless otherwise specified; do not reassign
  these streams.
  - You must pass the mandatory tests; failure to pass them results in an automatic zero for the
  submission.
  - Playing field coverage must be axisymmetric with respect to the southwest–northeast axis; this
  symmetry applies only to cover, not to ships.
  - Second command-line parameter is the playing-field side length; it must be at least 5 and odd.
  - A die roll must always be computed as random.nextInt(6) + 1.
  - nextInt should only be called when a die roll is actually required, to preserve the
  deterministic sequence.
  - Comments must be written consistently in either English or German.
  - Faulty module configurations must be detected as early as possible; on detection an informative
  error is printed and configuration for that ship is re-asked; previously correct ships are not
  re-queried.
  - A Collector always has exactly one Engine module and otherwise only the special Container
  module.
