  - Always destroy all additional modules first (for Sammler: Container modules), then destroy the
  Engine.
  - All submitted code must compile without errors.
  - Program outputs must exactly match the specification including case, spaces, and newlines for
  automated tests.
  - The mandatory tests must be passed before other tests are evaluated.
  - Comments should be uniformly written either in English or German.
  - Calls to System.exit(), Runtime.exit() or similar must not be used.
  - Do not reassign the standard streams System.in or System.out.
  - Error messages should clearly indicate why an input was rejected.
  - Every error message must begin with 'Error,' and must not contain special characters such as
  newlines or umlauts.
  - The user interface must be case-insensitive with respect to user input.
  </adaptive_rules>

