  <memories>
    - task.md describes the Abschlussaufgabe 2 AlphaZeta (AZ).
    - AlphaZeta (AZ) is a turn-based two-player strategy board game played on a square tile grid.
    - task.md specifies the implementation order: Spiellogik (game logic) before
  Benutzerschnittstelle (user interface)
    - Alpha controls ships A, B, C, D (A is the Collector); Zeta controls ships Z, W, X, Y (Z is the
   Collector).
    - Zeta controls ships Z, W, X, Y (Z is the Collector).
    - The assignment is part of the course 'Programmieren'.
    - The assignment is for Sommersemester 2022.
    - Attack ships have Engine as first module; per-ship limits: ≤2 weapon modules, ≤1 Rail Gun, ≤1
  Propulsion, ≤1 Shield; per fleet maximum 1 Sensor.
    - Action and movement rules: each module action can be used once per turn (per module);
  duplicate modules allow repeated use; move uses Manhattan distance and cannot target a tile
  occupied by cover or another ship; Propulsion allows a second move in the same turn; ramm can only
   be used if the attacker has no weapon modules, not against Collectors, and ramm can be used only
  once per ship per turn.
    - AI A is tasked to extract resources from the Asteroid Belt while contesting AI Z.
    - Attack resolution: attacker rolls a six-sided die, subtracts target cover and Shield effect
  (Shield reduces attack by 1); the result determines miss, hit, or critical hit and module
  destruction; when modules are destroyed, auxiliary modules are removed first (for Collector:
  Container), then the Engine; normally the defender chooses which modules are lost, but if the
  target is marked or the hit is critical the attacker chooses.
  </memories>
  <knowledge>
    - Otherwise module destruction is decided via dialog: '<Decider> must select <N> of <Ship>s
  module(s) (separated by comma):' and module choices listed alphabetically.
    - Ramm, Longshot and Strike use an initial attack die roll (six-sided 1–6), minus target cover,
  then apply Shield effect (−1 if target has Shield).
    - Die Methode nextInt darf nur dann aufgerufen werden, wenn tatsächlich ein Würfelwurf
  durchgeführt wird.
    - Die Seitenlänge (zweiter Parameter) muss mindestens 5 und ungerade sein.
    - Keine leere Kachel darf vollständig von Deckung umgeben sein; direkte Nachbarn dürfen nicht
  alle von Deckung belegt sein.
    - Distanzen werden als Manhattan-Distanz d1 = |xa−xb| + |ya−yb| berechnet; direkte Nachbarn
  haben d1 = 1.
    - Es darf nur eine einzige feste Instanz dieses Zufallszahlengenerators verwendet werden.
    - JavaDoc documentation rules must be followed and the JavaDoc @author tag must contain only the
   student's u-Kürzel.
    - Move target tile must not be occupied by cover or another ship.
    - Half cover reduces the die roll by 1; full cover reduces by 2.
    - Ramm may only be used if the attacking ship has no weapon modules.
    - Move requires no attack die roll.
    - Source code must obey a maximum line width of 120 characters.
    - All whitespace rules and naming rules for variables, methods and packages must be followed.
    - Appropriate visibilities must be chosen for classes, methods and attributes.
